infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title WAF paranoia level: permissive vs strict
  desc OWASP CRS blocks at anomaly score >= 5 — raising the paranoia level buys attack coverage at the cost of false positives
  compares
    - label PL1 — permissive (fewer rules active)
      children
        - label ~70% attack coverage
          desc Fewest rules fire, so obfuscated and novel attacks slip through
        - label ~0.1% legitimate requests blocked
          desc Near-zero false positives — safe to leave on without breaking real users
        - label Start here in detection mode
          desc Log and alert for 1-2 weeks to baseline scores before ever blocking
    - label PL4 — strict (most rules active)
      children
        - label ~95% attack coverage
          desc Most rules fire, catching obfuscated patterns PL1 misses
        - label ~5% legitimate requests blocked
          desc 50x the PL1 false-positive rate — a flood of support tickets from real users
        - label Tune before reaching here
          desc Whitelist false positives and adjust scoring; target 95% coverage at under 0.1% blocked
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
